{
 "about": "zoom-cut kinds: the numbers behind every version of the zoom-cut transition (motion-kit shelf/transitions/zoom-cut.jsx; EffectCraft transition.apply reads the same file). Measured on real editors' cuts (Rebuilds/hf-demos/zoom-research) and rebuilt in Rebuilds/hf-demos/zoom-versions (approved by Elias 4 Nov 2026). Plain data, no code.",
 "schema": {
  "time": "every t / in / out / land is SECONDS relative to the cut (the new layer's first frame); a caller snaps at + t to its comp's frames (round). One exception: an OLD-layer key at -1 reference frame or later (before the cut) goes on the last frame before the cut at any fps (a Launch out's peak on the last old frame; in seconds it would land 2 frames early at 60 fps and freeze that frame)",
  "fps / cutFrame / frames": "the reference's frame rate (exact, as a fraction string), the cut's frame index and the length of the approved demo comp",
  "layers": "old (outgoing shot), new (incoming shot) or window (into-window's window precomp): rest = the scale % the layer rests at; effects in stack order, each {name (the layer gets 'ZoomCut <kind> <name>'), effect id, set {param: value}, keys {param: track}, centre?}",
  "track": "{t: [s], v: [values], ease: [one per segment: a Graph name | 'linear' | {out, in} custom influence % | {outSpeed, outInfluence, inSpeed, inInfluence} units/s], zoom? (a scale: multiplied by restScale / rest), offset? (a position added to the zoom centre), steps? ('twos': holds every 2 comp frames, phase: the cut shows the frame before it), fit? (evidence)}",
  "centre": "the Transform effect's anchor = position, in px of a 1920x1080 layer (scaled to the layer's real size); default [960, 540]",
  "restLayer": "the layer restScale overrides (default new)",
  "comp": "comp settings the version needs (motion blur samples for the Transform shutter): raised, never lowered",
  "overlays": "extra layers: solid / light (solid + Gradient Ramp) / adjustment, placed above 'new' or above both shots ('top'), px of a 1920x1080 comp",
  "colours": "#rrggbb",
  "energy": "calm | medium | high",
  "land": "when the move has settled (s after the cut): the <id>-land hit",
  "demo": "the approved demo's footage: old/new 'from' = source seconds shown at the layer's in-point, old 'in' = its in-point in reference frames from comp start; top = which shot is above"
 },
